Confirmed API: `App#default` decorator registers the fallback handler invoked when no subcommand is given, `App#command` registers subcommands, and `App()` (via `__call__`) runs the app.

```python
from cyclopts import App

app = App(name="service", help="Manage the service.")


@app.command
def start():
    """Start the service."""
    print("Starting service...")


@app.command
def stop():
    """Stop the service."""
    print("Stopping service...")


@app.default
def status():
    """Show service status (runs when no subcommand is given)."""
    print("Service status: OK")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    app()
